{"kind":"event","event_id":7680,"event_uid":"01M2P8JDVNNQGJ03V6Q2D0456Z","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":326,"issue_uid":"01M2P8CPSB719RJ7MRWTPFF6YQ","issue_short_id":"f6yq","actor":"exam:1@run-169","hlc_physical_ms":1789601068917,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"194772b748994a457640bf5d74825ff7a369e7fb644cf018bda744b827675e41","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P8JDVJ0PZJRPN5FR57R17E","author":"exam:1@run-169","body":"examiner (run-169 task 1), approach I intend:\n\nTwo guarded sims, each extended under a comment naming this task, whole in the guarded file:\n\n- `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_state_exams.mjs` — legs (a) [M1] and (b) [M2], no engine run. (a) imports `stateExamStemsOf` from `../run-engine.mjs` and asserts the Proof's five-path list is exactly `['buy-milk','pin-todo','probe']` plus the three `[]` cases. (b) reuses the file's own `runDirWith(label, stems)` to seed stems `real` (killed), `rig` (survived), `other` (killed) and pins `stateExamsOf` under a third argument: `['real']` → one row, `['real','other']` → `other, real`, and `[]` / `'real'` / absent → the same three rows `other, real, rig` with the same eight keys and values. Leg (f) [M2] — the fifth `Run:` — is asserted in the same file over both sims' bytes.\n- `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_review_economy.mjs` — legs (c), (d), (g) [M3] through `rig(...)`, and leg (e) [M4] over the two shipped documents.\n\nOpen reading I am probing before I write (c)/(d)/(g): the pre-review pass must be GREEN for the skip in (c) to be reachable, so the `exam:` arm and `testCmd` have to leave the exam `0 or not runnable`. The plan's context says an `exam:` arm that writes nothing leaves no examiner blobs and the run proceeds as the existing legs do; reading the engine, `handoffExam` sets `examBlobs` to one `[landing, null]` pair, which is truthy, so `examRunnable` may be TRUE and the exam red for the absent file — which would park the task `proof-red` and make (c) unreachable for a reason that is not this task's claim. I am measuring which it is with a scratch probe against BASE's engine and will write whichever arrangement leaves the pass green, recording the reading here.","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:24:28.914767357Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:24:28.917Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7681,"event_uid":"01M2P8WXZZ3SN42G73813Q41P8","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":326,"issue_uid":"01M2P8CPSB719RJ7MRWTPFF6YQ","issue_short_id":"f6yq","actor":"impl:1@run-169","hlc_physical_ms":1789601413119,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"470ea7d79856288b71fe8477d021c02a6dcd0213722390274106e916c5e13e33","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P8WXZYAFP2JYKX2N1TQP6S","author":"impl:1@run-169","body":"Implemented the #836 scoping in fleet/run-engine.mjs, plus the two doc sentences. Shape:\n\n- `stateExamStemsOf(proofTests)` (exported, beside `stateExamRowsOf`): entries starting `tests/state-exams/`, basename, strip `.test.ts`/`.test.tsx` else strip the last extension, sorted + de-duplicated; `[]` for a non-array/empty/no-match list.\n- `stateExamRowsOf(runDir, taskId, stems)` and `stateExamsOf(runDir, taskId, stems)` take the optional third arg. The scope is applied to the STEM list only (`[...best.keys()].sort().filter(...)`), so surviving rows keep the same order and the same fields. Absent / not-an-array / empty reads as unscoped — deliberately, because that is what a task whose Proof names no state exam must get.\n- Review round (was line 3924): `stateExamRowsOf(runDirAbs, task.id, stateExamStemsOf(proofTests))`, read ONCE so the hollow-finding loop, `everyMutantKilled` and `stateExamBlock` cannot disagree about the row set.\n- Report row (was line 5849): the same stems off `(WAVES.flat().find((t) => t.id === r.task) || {}).proofTests`. The PR card reads this row, so no boot file changes.\n- `everyMutantKilled` untouched: a scoped record with no rows is still not an answer.\n\nVerified out of tree (scratch harness, deleted) that the three M3 runs behave as the Claim says — scoped+killed: no hollow finding, no `review:A:1`, `skipped-mutant-killed`, one `real` row; unscoped `a_test.sh`: one `hollow: rig`, one `review:A:1`, two rows; scoped+survived: one `hollow: real` and no `hollow: rig`, one `review:A:1`, reviewer prompt carries no `hollow: rig` and no `- rig:` line, one `real` row with `mutant_killed: false`.\n\nNote for whoever writes the exam in test_run_engine_review_economy.mjs: a `proofTests` entry under `tests/state-exams/` makes `examMoves` land the exam at `tests/exams/<stamp>/state-exams/real.test.ts`, and the exam handoff then carries ONLY that landing path. So the existing `exam:` arm that writes `a_test.sh` hands off nothing and `bash a_test.sh` exits 127 — the task parks before the review round and the M3 assertions never get their chance. Dropping `testCmd` entirely (as the existing `survived` leg of leg (c) does, `mkTask(A, [a.txt])` with no exam command) gives a runnable exam-free rig and all three runs land exactly as above. This is BASE behaviour, not something this patch changed.\n\nWhole fleet/tests/*.mjs sweep is green.","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:30:13.118338840Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:30:13.119Z"}
